WEBVTT

00:00:03.640 --> 00:00:07.560
<i>I, Koyuki Seri, was so aggravated 
by my easily provoked personality</i>

00:00:07.560 --> 00:00:11.000
<i>that I didn't notice I was walking
in front of an oncoming truck.</i>

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:30.350
<b>A Destructive God Sits Next to Me</b>

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:45.830
<b><i>Delusion 5</i></b>

00:01:43.220 --> 00:01:46.120
<i>How did I get into this mess, anyway?</i>

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:50.260
<i>That planning meeting ran way late.</i>

00:01:49.040 --> 00:01:50.250
<b>Mitoya High</b>

00:01:50.250 --> 00:01:51.960
<b>W\hH\hA\hM</b>

00:01:52.080 --> 00:01:54.800
All right, you're coming home with me.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:56.850
Stop struggling.

00:01:54.800 --> 00:01:57.740
Hold up! What's happening?!
Let me go! Let me go right now!

00:01:58.210 --> 00:02:01.640
Aww, I thought I'd caught a Sasquatch,
 but it was just Seri-kun.

00:02:01.640 --> 00:02:03.710
You did <i>not</i> think I was a Sasquatch!

00:02:03.710 --> 00:02:06.420
Your tea's getting cold.
This is an expensive Earl Grey.

00:02:06.420 --> 00:02:08.020
Then let me out of here already!

00:02:08.820 --> 00:02:12.060
<i>Jeez, what is he plotting now?</i>

00:02:12.400 --> 00:02:13.440
<i>And...</i>

00:02:13.440 --> 00:02:16.650
<b>Cerberus</b>

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:16.750
<i>What on earth is he making Hanadori-kun do?</i>

00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:18.260
What?

00:02:18.640 --> 00:02:20.200
Cerberus ran away?

00:02:20.200 --> 00:02:21.730
That's right.

00:02:21.730 --> 00:02:24.350
I have two pets. There's Cerberus,
 the dog Hanadori gave me,

00:02:24.350 --> 00:02:27.400
and my cat, Schrödinger.

00:02:27.400 --> 00:02:29.160
<i>That cat looks familiar...</i>

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:33.080
<i>Play, play, play! Hey! Let's play!</i>

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:33.080
Schrödinger always ignores Cerberus 
when he tries to get him to play,

00:02:33.090 --> 00:02:36.590
until he finally hauls off 
and kicks him in the face.

00:02:33.320 --> 00:02:35.650
<i>Get lost, mutt!</i>

00:02:36.590 --> 00:02:38.350
<i>That sounds oddly familiar...</i>

00:02:38.350 --> 00:02:41.380
So then Cerberus runs off.

00:02:41.380 --> 00:02:45.030
I don't usually worry because 
he always comes back...

00:02:45.030 --> 00:02:46.880
<i>You were laughing your ass off, I bet.</i>

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:48.760
But he didn't come home this time.

00:02:49.080 --> 00:02:52.710
So I asked Hanadori to try 
and think like Cerberus,

00:02:52.710 --> 00:02:54.900
but it isn't helping.

00:02:54.900 --> 00:02:56.230
<i>Learn how to say no!</i>

00:02:56.230 --> 00:02:58.030
<i>Is he really serious 
about looking for him?</i>

00:02:58.030 --> 00:03:00.950
Gosh, I wonder where Cerberus is now...

00:03:01.140 --> 00:03:02.940
Did he get lost?

00:03:02.940 --> 00:03:05.040
Did someone dognap him?

00:03:05.040 --> 00:03:09.150
What if he got into an accident somewhere?

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:11.750
Cerberus!

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:13.520
<i>He's so creepy when he cries!</i>

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:17.300
Cerberus! Cerberus!

00:03:14.570 --> 00:03:17.300
<i>Damn. This is always how it ends.</i>

00:03:17.300 --> 00:03:19.460
<i>I wanted to go home and study.</i>

00:03:19.790 --> 00:03:21.500
<i>Well, whatever...</i>

00:03:21.600 --> 00:03:24.790
Is there some place he'd probably go?

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:27.780
Whenever I take him for walks,

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:30.740
he always chases things
that resemble Hanadori.

00:03:30.740 --> 00:03:31.610
Resemble him?

00:03:31.610 --> 00:03:35.080
He'll go after anything that sort of
 looks like Hanadori's eyepatch.

00:03:35.080 --> 00:03:37.500
<i>Is he smart, stupid, or a moron?</i>

00:03:37.500 --> 00:03:39.080
<i>Why doesn't he use his nose?</i>

00:03:39.080 --> 00:03:44.140
In that case, if we hang Hanadori-kun
by the front door, then eventually...

00:03:44.140 --> 00:03:45.520
I already tried that.

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:46.370
<i>You did?</i>

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:49.580
All right! If we look for things
that resemble Hanadori,

00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:51.930
we're likely to find Cerberus.

00:03:51.930 --> 00:03:53.330
Let's split up and search!

00:03:53.330 --> 00:03:54.340
Yeah!

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:56.670
<i>"Things that resemble Hanadori"
is pretty broad, though...</i>

00:03:56.980 --> 00:03:59.400
Cerberus! Cerberus!

00:03:59.450 --> 00:04:04.400
<i>But the little fella really 
liked Hanadori-kun, huh?</i>

00:04:00.250 --> 00:04:03.480
Cerberus! Cerberus!

00:04:04.880 --> 00:04:06.360
<i>No wonder he's fond of him.</i>

00:04:06.360 --> 00:04:07.840
Cerberus!

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:09.990
<i>Okay!</i>

00:04:10.360 --> 00:04:11.620
Cerberus!

00:04:11.620 --> 00:04:12.920
Cerberus!

00:04:12.920 --> 00:04:14.430
<i>What an embarrassing name!</i>

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:15.650
Cerberus!

00:04:15.650 --> 00:04:16.770
Welcome!

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:17.170
<b><i>Milk Frappuccino</i></b>

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:18.130
<b><i>New Item</i></b>

00:04:16.770 --> 00:04:18.130
<i>Enjoy the rich
aroma of milk!</i>

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:18.130
Cerberus!

00:04:18.130 --> 00:04:20.360
A milk frappuccino, then?

00:04:20.710 --> 00:04:22.280
Cerberus!

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:23.410
<i>Why are you the only one not
looking?! He's </i>your<i> dog!</i>

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:24.580
Cerberus!

00:04:25.240 --> 00:04:29.040
Even with all my power,
I failed to find him, huh?

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:32.660
My third eye cannot function when 
the sun dips below the horizon...

00:04:32.660 --> 00:04:35.200
<i>The dark god of destruction is night blind?</i>

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:38.250
Oh? Hey, isn't that...

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:39.250
Hibiki-kun?

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:41.080
What's he doing there?

00:04:41.080 --> 00:04:43.960
Oh, you've got great taste!

00:04:43.960 --> 00:04:46.930
That's a real hit with all the cool kids.

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:49.980
If you wear it, you'll be cool, too!

00:04:50.220 --> 00:04:51.660
Really?

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:54.640
Will I be like Miguel-senpai?

00:04:54.640 --> 00:04:57.160
Yeah, of course! No idea who that is, but sure.

00:04:57.160 --> 00:04:58.920
May I try it on?

00:04:58.920 --> 00:04:59.980
<i>Don't tell me...</i>

00:05:00.820 --> 00:05:02.560
Yup, that's it.

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:04.570
I bought mine at that shop, too.

00:05:04.570 --> 00:05:06.320
<i>I really don't care about that.</i>

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:09.370
<i>Anyway, if Cerberus is anywhere nearby...</i>

00:05:09.370 --> 00:05:10.280
<i>Like right there!</i>

00:05:15.370 --> 00:05:16.200
Cerberus!

00:05:16.200 --> 00:05:17.090
Hup!

00:05:22.380 --> 00:05:24.020
Gestöber!

00:05:25.460 --> 00:05:26.840
<i>Oh, right...</i>

00:05:26.840 --> 00:05:28.500
<i>That's what happened.</i>

00:05:29.440 --> 00:05:31.630
<i>I guess Cerberus is safe.</i>

00:05:29.900 --> 00:05:32.060
Gestöber! Gestöber!

00:05:33.070 --> 00:05:34.600
<i>What a relief.</i>

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:38.350
<i>Now I won't have to see any more
of Hanadori-kun's creepy crying.</i>

00:05:38.350 --> 00:05:39.830
<i>I'm really glad...</i>

00:05:40.640 --> 00:05:42.200
<i>Wait, no I'm not!</i>

00:05:42.200 --> 00:05:45.140
<i>I know it was kind of my fault,
but this isn't fair!</i>

00:05:45.140 --> 00:05:47.660
<i>What's even happening?
This is fantasy, not comedy!</i>

00:05:47.660 --> 00:05:49.700
<i>I can see myself lying on the ground...</i>

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:51.870
<i>Is this an out-of-body experience?</i>

00:05:51.870 --> 00:05:55.590
<i>If this floating thing is severed, will I...</i>

00:05:55.590 --> 00:05:57.470
<i>No! I don't want to die!</i>

00:05:57.470 --> 00:05:59.040
<i>Somebody save me!</i>

00:05:59.040 --> 00:06:00.630
G-Gestöber...

00:06:00.630 --> 00:06:02.120
He's out cold.

00:06:02.120 --> 00:06:03.840
Gestöber, wake up!

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:04.960
<b>KA-POW</b>

00:06:03.840 --> 00:06:04.970
Bad!

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:06.950
Don't shake him, Hanadori.

00:06:07.550 --> 00:06:10.760
I don't see any injuries,
but he may have hit his head.

00:06:10.760 --> 00:06:13.440
If he has a concussion,
 we may need to cool his head...

00:06:13.440 --> 00:06:15.550
But I don't have any real training.

00:06:16.090 --> 00:06:18.220
The only thing we can do now is...

00:06:18.540 --> 00:06:23.040
Use the ultimate dark destruction and
revival secret technique, Wiederbelebung?

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:23.820
<i>Wrong.</i>

00:06:24.030 --> 00:06:26.280
<i>I don't even know what that is,
but I know it's not right!</i>

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:29.300
<i>This is an emergency!
Why are you acting like that?</i>

00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:35.720
Maybe Seri-kun should stop floating
around and go back into his body?

00:06:35.720 --> 00:06:37.000
<i>He can see me?!</i>

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:39.200
<i>Anything goes with Tsukimiya-kun, huh?</i>

00:06:39.200 --> 00:06:41.880
Can't you just, like, zoom right back in?

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:43.500
<i>I don't know...</i>

00:06:47.970 --> 00:06:49.980
<i>Gah! Why can't I get back in?!</i>

00:06:50.130 --> 00:06:52.680
If I pull this cord thing and then let go,

00:06:52.680 --> 00:06:56.310
maybe it'll retract like a 
vacuum cleaner cord does.

00:06:57.290 --> 00:06:58.680
<i>Abort! Abort!</i>

00:06:58.680 --> 00:07:01.280
<i>I'm scared that first yank
will rip it out, so don't!</i>

00:07:01.500 --> 00:07:03.260
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:07:03.260 --> 00:07:04.300
I knew it...

00:07:04.300 --> 00:07:07.120
Disaster follows me everywhere I go.

00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:08.860
Why?

00:07:08.860 --> 00:07:09.450
<i>Ack!</i>

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:13.590
Please, God! Spare Senpai 
and take me instead!

00:07:12.820 --> 00:07:13.590
<i>Spare me!</i>

00:07:13.590 --> 00:07:16.170
<i>You're gonna cut it!
You'll be a real grim reaper!</i>

00:07:16.760 --> 00:07:19.220
It's not working...
I need more spiritual power!

00:07:19.230 --> 00:07:20.750
<i>I'm not expecting much. Don't worry.</i>

00:07:20.750 --> 00:07:23.420
<i>Go gather seven balls to 
grant your wish or something.</i>

00:07:23.420 --> 00:07:25.250
You mean Seririn?!

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:27.630
<i>Shut up! That joke's way 
too old for anyone to get!</i>

00:07:27.630 --> 00:07:31.410
<i>It's no use... I was stupid
to count on them for help.</i>

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:34.350
<i>My consciousness is fading...</i>

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:36.100
<i>Am I going to die?</i>

00:07:38.700 --> 00:07:43.760
<i>I knew it. Nothing good comes 
from hanging around these people.</i>

00:07:48.860 --> 00:07:52.230
<i>What's going to happen after I'm gone?</i>

00:07:52.990 --> 00:07:56.560
<i>I'm sure it won't change a thing...</i>

00:07:56.560 --> 00:07:57.950
No!

00:07:57.950 --> 00:08:00.920
Wake up, Gestöber!

00:08:01.300 --> 00:08:03.890
Gestöber! Gestöber!

00:08:04.240 --> 00:08:06.220
Gestöber!

00:08:07.550 --> 00:08:09.140
<i>Hanadori-kun...</i>

00:08:10.480 --> 00:08:11.470
Hanadori!

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:13.020
His hand just moved a little!

00:08:13.020 --> 00:08:15.560
And the color saturation of 
his face improved by 1%!

00:08:15.560 --> 00:08:16.790
<i>What? Color saturation?</i>

00:08:16.790 --> 00:08:19.270
It means your pallor improved a little.

00:08:19.270 --> 00:08:22.210
The tears of those you care 
about can wake you up.

00:08:22.210 --> 00:08:23.990
It really works!

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:26.440
<b>S</b>

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:26.440
<b>H</b>

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:26.440
<b>O</b>

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:26.440
<b>C</b>

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:26.440
<b>K</b>

00:08:23.990 --> 00:08:26.440
Just like you always see in manga!

00:08:26.440 --> 00:08:30.450
Let those holy drops fall
upon Seri-kun's face, Hanadori!

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:31.270
All right.

00:08:31.270 --> 00:08:32.160
<i>Don't!</i>

00:08:32.160 --> 00:08:34.740
<i>No dark god of destruction juice, please!</i>

00:08:35.370 --> 00:08:37.710
It's no use! He's not waking up!

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:39.260
<i>My face! No!</i>

00:08:39.260 --> 00:08:43.760
<i>I don't want to wake up like this!</i>

00:08:42.110 --> 00:08:44.190
So we need to move on to the next cliché.

00:08:44.800 --> 00:08:46.170
The next cliché?

00:08:46.170 --> 00:08:47.890
<i>No! I have a terrible feeling about—</i>

00:08:47.890 --> 00:08:49.250
A prince's kiss...

00:08:49.250 --> 00:08:51.470
Kiss...

00:08:53.330 --> 00:08:55.440
A-All right.

00:08:55.440 --> 00:08:57.070
Have faith, Hanadori!

00:08:57.070 --> 00:08:59.050
With Sturmhut's powers of light,

00:08:59.050 --> 00:09:00.640
I know you can save him!

00:09:00.640 --> 00:09:03.850
Miguel-senpai, please save Gestöber-senpai!

00:09:05.970 --> 00:09:07.310
<i>No, no, no!</i>

00:09:25.080 --> 00:09:26.330
<b>G\hR\hA\hB</b>

00:09:26.850 --> 00:09:27.920
<i>Wait, what?</i>

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:29.740
Hey, you okay, kid?

00:09:27.920 --> 00:09:29.740
<i>I...</i>

00:09:29.740 --> 00:09:31.820
I'm glad you woke up, Seri-kun!

00:09:29.740 --> 00:09:31.820
You might have a mild concussion.

00:09:31.820 --> 00:09:33.770
Cer-chan's safe, too, Senpai!

00:09:34.710 --> 00:09:36.230
<i>I'm back...</i>

00:09:38.680 --> 00:09:40.640
<i>Thank goodness!</i>

00:09:39.030 --> 00:09:40.640
<b>Droop</b>

00:09:40.640 --> 00:09:43.650
Good thing that truck stopped
 before it hit you, huh?

00:09:43.650 --> 00:09:44.250
What?

00:09:44.250 --> 00:09:46.100
You don't remember, Seri-kun?

00:09:46.100 --> 00:09:47.940
You saved Cerberus,

00:09:47.940 --> 00:09:49.270
the truck stopped,

00:09:49.270 --> 00:09:51.070
and everything was fine.

00:09:51.070 --> 00:09:54.800
But then Hanadori jumped 
at you for some reason.

00:09:52.920 --> 00:09:54.800
<b>Slam</b>

00:09:54.800 --> 00:09:56.640
That's how you got knocked out.

00:09:56.640 --> 00:09:58.870
No more running into traffic, okay?

00:09:59.140 --> 00:10:02.320
<i>That nearly killed me?</i>

00:10:03.060 --> 00:10:06.340
<i>These guys aren't just annoying...</i>

00:10:06.340 --> 00:10:08.470
<i>They're a huge pain in the ass!</i>

00:10:08.850 --> 00:10:11.160
W-Wait, Gestöber.

00:10:11.160 --> 00:10:13.240
You need to see a doctor.

00:10:13.240 --> 00:10:14.000
<i>Yes, I know.</i>

00:10:14.000 --> 00:10:15.660
<i>Whose fault do you think that is?</i>

00:10:16.790 --> 00:10:19.000
Gestöber, I-I'm sorry.

00:10:19.000 --> 00:10:22.780
Just take Cerberus and go home.

00:10:22.780 --> 00:10:26.640
<i>I know he was trying to save me
and didn't mean any harm.</i>

00:10:27.100 --> 00:10:29.770
<i>But I've decided I'm never
hanging out with him again.</i>

00:10:29.770 --> 00:10:31.020
<i>Ever!</i>

00:10:32.700 --> 00:10:35.920
I'm glad you found Cerberus.

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:41.660
G-Gestöber!

00:10:41.860 --> 00:10:43.280
<i>So creepy!</i>

00:10:43.280 --> 00:10:44.960
I'm sorry!

00:10:45.620 --> 00:10:48.340
Miguel-senpai...

00:10:50.000 --> 00:10:51.300
<i>Well...</i>

00:10:51.300 --> 00:10:55.150
<i>I'll guess I'll hang out with him
just enough to keep him from crying.</i>

00:10:57.900 --> 00:10:59.880
You've got the basics down,

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:01.820
<b>Koyuki</b>

00:10:59.880 --> 00:11:02.840
so you'll start today, Koyuki-kun.

00:11:02.840 --> 00:11:03.600
Okay!

00:11:03.600 --> 00:11:05.640
Remember, the customers are gods.

00:11:05.640 --> 00:11:08.680
But be confident, and don't do anything rude.

00:11:08.680 --> 00:11:09.680
Good luck.

00:11:10.460 --> 00:11:13.520
Party of two, dark god of destruct—

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:13.860
Dark God of Destruction
Miguel

00:11:12.150 --> 00:11:13.860
Yamada 

00:11:14.400 --> 00:11:16.390
<i>I just started a job at a chain restaurant,</i>

00:11:16.390 --> 00:11:19.140
<i>and the dark god of destruction 
has come to dine.</i>

00:11:20.030 --> 00:11:22.570
<i>Why?! Why are they here?</i>

00:11:22.570 --> 00:11:25.270
<i>I deliberately picked a place
far away from where we live!</i>

00:11:25.270 --> 00:11:26.780
<i>I decided to get this job</i>

00:11:26.780 --> 00:11:30.560
<i>so I could buy Sumiso-san a 
present for her birthday...</i>

00:11:30.560 --> 00:11:34.100
<i>But I apparently can't do anything
without them coming to screw it up!</i>

00:11:34.100 --> 00:11:36.440
Hey, show them to their table already.

00:11:39.140 --> 00:11:40.760
Here you are.

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:42.110
Long belt wrapped up too tight

00:11:40.760 --> 00:11:42.410
Nametag hidden by menu

00:11:41.220 --> 00:11:44.300
Your hand towels and water.

00:11:42.110 --> 00:11:44.680
Funny face and glasses

00:11:42.410 --> 00:11:44.680
Unkempt hair
with hat pulled down

00:11:45.500 --> 00:11:46.630
<i>Gulp.</i>

00:11:47.940 --> 00:11:49.730
<i>I-I knew this would never work...</i>

00:11:52.030 --> 00:11:54.560
A seasonal yam parfait!

00:11:54.340 --> 00:11:57.390
<i>Th-Thank God, my cover's not blown.</i>

00:11:54.560 --> 00:11:56.920
A new menu item!

00:11:57.390 --> 00:11:59.250
<i>I guess the dark god of
destruction has a sweet too—</i>

00:11:58.520 --> 00:12:01.990
And now it's time for the 
Seri-kun, a.k.a. Gestöber, quiz!

00:11:59.070 --> 00:12:01.990
<b>Freeze</b>

00:12:02.280 --> 00:12:03.950
<i>Tsukimiya-kun... What is this?!</i>

00:12:03.950 --> 00:12:08.540
What does Seri-kun have at home that 
he's treasured since he was a boy?

00:12:10.540 --> 00:12:12.630
A stuffed cat named Nyanteko!

00:12:13.230 --> 00:12:14.410
That's right!

00:12:14.410 --> 00:12:15.820
<i>That's not what the buzzer's for!</i>

00:12:15.820 --> 00:12:17.680
<i>And how do you know about that?!</i>

00:12:17.680 --> 00:12:19.560
<i>The buzzer's for placing your order!</i>

00:12:19.560 --> 00:12:20.630
<i>It's not a toy!</i>

00:12:21.010 --> 00:12:25.040
S-Sir, you're bothering the other customers...

00:12:25.040 --> 00:12:26.410
Oh, can I order now?

00:12:26.410 --> 00:12:27.720
<i>You're ordering?</i>

00:12:27.720 --> 00:12:30.540
I'll have the piping-hot Hamburg
steak doria with the drink bar.

00:12:30.540 --> 00:12:32.430
<i>What about the seasonal yam parfait?</i>

00:12:32.430 --> 00:12:33.900
<i>No, I have to calm down...</i>

00:12:33.900 --> 00:12:35.640
<i>He's a customer.</i>

00:12:35.640 --> 00:12:38.340
<i>If I yell at him like usual, 
I'll get fired on the spot!</i>

00:12:38.340 --> 00:12:39.550
...over...

00:12:40.630 --> 00:12:43.070
<i>Crap! He's onto me!</i>

00:12:43.070 --> 00:12:45.630
Um, I knocked this over. Can I get a napkin?

00:12:45.630 --> 00:12:48.790
<i>I thought you were saying "Gestöber," damn it!</i>

00:12:49.430 --> 00:12:51.860
<i>Has he really not figured me out?</i>

00:12:51.860 --> 00:12:53.180
<i>Am I in the clear?</i>

00:12:53.790 --> 00:12:56.620
<i>This guy's definitely figured 
me out, though... Damn it.</i>

00:12:57.490 --> 00:12:59.290
I'm already exhausted...

00:13:00.440 --> 00:13:01.740
Here you go.

00:13:01.740 --> 00:13:03.680
Your piping-hot Hamburg steak doria.

00:13:03.680 --> 00:13:06.760
The dish is extremely hot, so...

00:13:07.440 --> 00:13:09.640
<i>Please listen to your waiter, sir.</i>

00:13:09.800 --> 00:13:11.240
<i>Damn it! It's hopeless!</i>

00:13:11.240 --> 00:13:13.740
<i>I just need to think about
the other customers!</i>

00:13:14.400 --> 00:13:17.200
<i>I'm doing this for the sake
 of my bright future!</i>

00:13:17.970 --> 00:13:19.360
Welcome!

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:22.460
Would this table be all right, miss?

00:13:22.460 --> 00:13:23.560
No.

00:13:24.120 --> 00:13:26.780
Some freak is sitting there.

00:13:27.030 --> 00:13:31.080
Miguel, the gratin isn't just hot outside...
It's hot on the inside, too.

00:13:31.080 --> 00:13:33.540
Just like your passion.

00:13:33.780 --> 00:13:38.720
<i>Oh, it's the weirdo who was
in a band with Hanadori-kun.</i>

00:13:38.880 --> 00:13:40.230
<i>Ah, damn it all!</i>

00:13:40.230 --> 00:13:41.490
<i>He caught me so off-guard</i>

00:13:41.490 --> 00:13:44.140
<i>that I just remembered a bunch
of stuff I didn't want to!</i>

00:13:44.520 --> 00:13:46.100
<i>What the heck is he doing?</i>

00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:48.250
<i>Did he come to get Hanadori-kun back again?</i>

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:50.550
Be careful, Miguel...

00:13:50.550 --> 00:13:52.500
Don't underestimate that macaroni.

00:13:52.500 --> 00:13:54.640
Slurp up what's inside it,

00:13:54.640 --> 00:13:58.060
and the sweet cream sauce
will explode onto your tongue.

00:13:58.060 --> 00:13:59.900
Don't rush.

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:02.260
Softly put it to your lips and feel it.

00:14:02.260 --> 00:14:04.940
Let it dribble into your 
naughty, greedy mouth...

00:14:04.570 --> 00:14:07.700
<i>Why does he make everything sound so creepy?</i>

00:14:04.940 --> 00:14:07.700
Yes, just like that, Miguel-kun...

00:14:07.700 --> 00:14:09.400
Pant on it to cool it down.

00:14:09.400 --> 00:14:10.410
<i>You mean "blow," right?</i>

00:14:10.810 --> 00:14:15.550
Shi-chan, if you're that worried
 about Miguel, then just tell him.

00:14:15.550 --> 00:14:16.380
<i>Who's he?</i>

00:14:16.680 --> 00:14:19.420
You're not focusing on rehearsals!

00:14:19.420 --> 00:14:20.440
Don't say that.

00:14:20.440 --> 00:14:22.290
I've already been defeated.

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:25.660
I'm no longer a bull, but a little lost sheep.

00:14:25.660 --> 00:14:29.020
Go ahead and laugh. I'm a coward.

00:14:29.630 --> 00:14:31.760
Satan of my soul!

00:14:31.760 --> 00:14:34.190
Return to me once more!

00:14:34.520 --> 00:14:35.660
It's ironic.

00:14:34.560 --> 00:14:38.050
<i>Sir, please refrain from any 
performances in our establishment.</i>

00:14:35.660 --> 00:14:39.150
I guess some gods only come
to you when you're hurt.

00:14:39.420 --> 00:14:40.110
<i>Sir?</i>

00:14:40.110 --> 00:14:41.680
I could write some great lyrics right now.

00:14:43.520 --> 00:14:46.160
Manager, can I work in the kitchen?

00:14:46.160 --> 00:14:47.360
You can't cook.

00:14:47.360 --> 00:14:48.900
Now get back to work.

00:14:49.670 --> 00:14:52.370
Um, party of one,

00:14:52.370 --> 00:14:53.800
Grim Reaper He—

00:14:53.800 --> 00:14:55.950
<i>Wow, the reaper's here, too.</i>

00:14:55.950 --> 00:14:58.730
<i>What the heck is this?
Why do they all come together?</i>

00:14:58.730 --> 00:15:01.670
<i>Is this a dark god of destruction
 meetup or something?</i>

00:15:02.880 --> 00:15:04.840
He looks funny!

00:15:04.840 --> 00:15:06.840
Shh! Don't look, Chikako!

00:15:08.220 --> 00:15:09.380
Sir...

00:15:09.380 --> 00:15:13.890
Is it that weird to go to a
restaurant by yourself?

00:15:13.890 --> 00:15:16.140
<i>I think it's more what you're holding, sir.</i>

00:15:16.140 --> 00:15:18.260
I'm not welcome here?

00:15:18.260 --> 00:15:19.510
Of course not...

00:15:19.510 --> 00:15:20.850
I'm the grim reaper.

00:15:20.850 --> 00:15:23.440
There's no place for me here!

00:15:21.600 --> 00:15:23.440
Sir!

00:15:24.510 --> 00:15:25.480
Koyuki-kun,

00:15:25.480 --> 00:15:28.430
you lose points for not making
the customer feel at home.

00:15:28.430 --> 00:15:30.150
That's not fair...

00:15:31.060 --> 00:15:34.110
<i>Can I really keep this job?</i>

00:15:35.460 --> 00:15:36.610
Oh, no!

00:15:36.610 --> 00:15:38.700
I don't know how to use the drink machine!

00:15:38.700 --> 00:15:41.920
My soda isn't going into my cup...

00:15:41.920 --> 00:15:43.170
That's strange...

00:15:43.420 --> 00:15:48.140
<i>Is he doing this because 
he actually knows it's me?</i>

00:15:48.400 --> 00:15:50.770
<i>He's a pain no matter where I go.</i>

00:15:50.770 --> 00:15:53.100
<i>I hope someone else helps him.</i>

00:15:53.100 --> 00:15:56.400
Mommy, I'm gonna get more ice cream!

00:16:01.530 --> 00:16:06.110
You came close to being struck 
by the spray of a dark weapon.

00:16:06.550 --> 00:16:08.360
Are you okay, little one?

00:16:08.360 --> 00:16:10.040
Uh-huh! I'm okay!

00:16:10.040 --> 00:16:11.440
<i>W-Wow.</i>

00:16:11.440 --> 00:16:14.130
<i>He's drenched in coffee, 
and he still looks like a hero...</i>

00:16:14.130 --> 00:16:14.820
<i>No, wait!</i>

00:16:14.870 --> 00:16:16.780
Are you all right, sir?

00:16:16.780 --> 00:16:17.690
Are you hurt?

00:16:17.690 --> 00:16:19.660
I'll bring you a cold towel.

00:16:19.660 --> 00:16:21.310
Are you okay, Onii-chan?

00:16:20.340 --> 00:16:22.240
<i>I'm sorry, Hanadori-kun.</i>

00:16:21.310 --> 00:16:22.620
Was it hot?

00:16:22.890 --> 00:16:24.980
<i>I couldn't move at all, but you...</i>

00:16:23.250 --> 00:16:27.760
After enduring the flames of hell, 
this was nothing.

00:16:27.760 --> 00:16:29.350
What's "hell"?

00:16:29.350 --> 00:16:30.580
That's a secret.

00:16:30.580 --> 00:16:33.600
It's a chaotic land of intense fire...

00:16:33.600 --> 00:16:35.600
And I am its ruler.

00:16:35.600 --> 00:16:38.640
Hey! What are you doing to my daughter?!

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:41.120
Y-Y-You've got it all wrong, ma'am.

00:16:41.120 --> 00:16:41.780
What?!

00:16:41.780 --> 00:16:44.440
Hanado— I mean, that boy 
tried to protect your daughter.

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:47.270
He was telling her a bunch of weird stuff!

00:16:47.270 --> 00:16:50.860
<i>Th-That's kind of the one and only 
thing that makes him special....</i>

00:16:49.480 --> 00:16:51.080
What's your problem?

00:16:51.080 --> 00:16:53.660
A part-timer talking back to a customer?

00:16:53.660 --> 00:16:56.940
Didn't you even learn to treat
your customers like gods?

00:16:57.400 --> 00:16:58.390
But...

00:16:58.390 --> 00:16:59.320
But what?!

00:17:00.050 --> 00:17:01.850
<i>This isn't fair at all.</i>

00:17:01.850 --> 00:17:02.750
<i>It's frustrating.</i>

00:17:02.750 --> 00:17:04.570
If customers are gods,

00:17:04.570 --> 00:17:07.000
then so are the wait staff.

00:17:07.000 --> 00:17:08.940
What? Who are you?

00:17:08.940 --> 00:17:10.600
A customer, like you.

00:17:10.600 --> 00:17:12.200
Let's talk as equals.

00:17:12.200 --> 00:17:13.210
<i>Tsukimiya-kun...</i>

00:17:13.210 --> 00:17:14.320
I'm the only god here.

00:17:14.320 --> 00:17:17.640
<i>Not now! You'll only make things worse!</i>

00:17:17.940 --> 00:17:20.140
I'm paying good money here!

00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:21.710
Money makes the world go 'round.

00:17:21.710 --> 00:17:24.440
So obviously, paying customers
 are the most important!

00:17:24.440 --> 00:17:27.850
But it's what your money can <i>get</i> you
that you actually want, right?

00:17:27.850 --> 00:17:29.880
Houses, cars, clothes,

00:17:29.880 --> 00:17:32.310
peace of mind, yummy food...

00:17:32.310 --> 00:17:35.730
Let's be grateful that we can
exchange our money for these things!

00:17:35.730 --> 00:17:38.010
Can you eat gratitude?

00:17:38.010 --> 00:17:39.660
Money will never betray you.

00:17:39.660 --> 00:17:41.240
It's more valuable than anything!

00:17:41.240 --> 00:17:43.460
What if the economy implodes

00:17:43.460 --> 00:17:46.440
and it's worth nothing more
than the paper it's printed on?

00:17:44.700 --> 00:17:47.960
U-Um, pardon me...

00:17:46.440 --> 00:17:48.710
What am I supposed to trust, then?

00:17:48.710 --> 00:17:50.210
Love, ma'am!

00:17:50.600 --> 00:17:51.600
You're a fool.

00:17:51.600 --> 00:17:53.760
Love is the least trustworthy thing of all.

00:17:53.760 --> 00:17:55.040
Just look at my husband!

00:17:55.040 --> 00:17:59.310
Your husband left home,
leaving you and your daughter behind...

00:17:59.660 --> 00:18:02.980
But how do you know it wasn't 
love that made him do it?

00:18:02.980 --> 00:18:04.770
Don't kid yourself!

00:18:04.770 --> 00:18:07.620
He got us into debt and 
doesn't pay child support.

00:18:07.620 --> 00:18:09.180
He's a total failure!

00:18:09.180 --> 00:18:13.140
He may have left you so you
wouldn't have to bear his burdens.

00:18:14.600 --> 00:18:15.990
That's...

00:18:17.210 --> 00:18:20.320
That's... just irresponsible.

00:18:20.320 --> 00:18:21.920
It is.

00:18:21.920 --> 00:18:28.300
But maybe it was love that drove 
him to such a desperate decision.

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:31.130
In his own awkward, messed-up way.

00:18:32.240 --> 00:18:33.550
You jerk...

00:18:33.550 --> 00:18:36.940
Why wouldn't you let us
 share the burden with you?

00:18:36.940 --> 00:18:37.980
Ma'am...

00:18:38.300 --> 00:18:39.780
It's love, isn't it?

00:18:39.780 --> 00:18:40.990
This is love!

00:18:40.990 --> 00:18:43.290
And you're a god!

00:18:43.290 --> 00:18:45.060
And you're a goddess!

00:18:45.060 --> 00:18:46.560
<i>What is even happening?</i>

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:50.500
My dark god is awakening!

00:18:51.040 --> 00:18:52.820
Awakening...

00:18:52.820 --> 00:18:55.820
Koyuki-kun, what's going on here?

00:18:55.820 --> 00:18:58.700
I'm sorry. I don't know, either.

00:18:59.190 --> 00:19:01.350
I'll call you, Utsugi-kun!

00:19:01.350 --> 00:19:04.020
Let's talk about love again soon!

00:19:04.020 --> 00:19:06.120
Bye-bye, Miguel-oniichan!

00:19:06.120 --> 00:19:08.000
Seal that dark god away, okay?

00:19:08.720 --> 00:19:10.420
<i>The storm has passed.</i>

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:13.460
<i>I'm so glad they never figured me out...</i>

00:19:12.520 --> 00:19:13.460
Koyuki-kun!

00:19:13.730 --> 00:19:17.700
Go give these to the customer that
got soaked with coffee and apologize.

00:19:13.940 --> 00:19:18.800
<b>Fluffy Pancake
 Discount Coupon</b>

00:19:17.700 --> 00:19:18.800
Okay.

00:19:19.000 --> 00:19:21.580
<i>Just when I thought I was in the clear.</i>

00:19:22.040 --> 00:19:23.110
<i>But...</i>

00:19:23.390 --> 00:19:26.760
<i>In the end, the two of them
 really helped me out.</i>

00:19:27.100 --> 00:19:29.380
<i>I couldn't have done any of that on my own.</i>

00:19:29.380 --> 00:19:31.190
<i>I need to thank them.</i>

00:19:31.380 --> 00:19:32.640
Sir!

00:19:33.200 --> 00:19:35.350
I'm not important enough
to give you my name.

00:19:35.350 --> 00:19:37.160
<i>Except you already did.</i>

00:19:37.160 --> 00:19:39.360
<i>You wrote it on the waiting list.</i>

00:19:41.790 --> 00:19:47.580
I-I apologize for the bad
experience you had today!

00:19:47.900 --> 00:19:51.750
You helped that little girl when we couldn't,

00:19:51.750 --> 00:19:52.680
so, um...

00:19:52.680 --> 00:19:54.060
Thank you!

00:19:54.060 --> 00:19:56.790
Please take these as 
our way of saying thanks.

00:19:58.100 --> 00:20:00.090
There's no need to apologize.

00:20:00.620 --> 00:20:02.400
Remember what Tsukimiya said?

00:20:02.400 --> 00:20:05.880
The customer and the staff should be equals.

00:20:06.680 --> 00:20:08.770
We'll gratefully accept these.

00:20:08.770 --> 00:20:10.490
And we'll come back soon.

00:20:10.490 --> 00:20:11.350
Thanks.

00:20:12.420 --> 00:20:15.280
I'm really sor—

00:20:16.280 --> 00:20:17.740
<i>Crap.</i>

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:24.250
I knew the whole time.

00:20:25.240 --> 00:20:29.000
What? Don't tell me you thought
 he didn't know, Seri-kun!

00:20:29.000 --> 00:20:30.080
Stop it, Tsukimiya.

00:20:30.180 --> 00:20:33.410
Gestöber was working and 
didn't want to be bothered,

00:20:33.410 --> 00:20:36.380
so he did his best to disguise himself
 and believed it had worked.

00:20:36.380 --> 00:20:38.560
Sure, he did a terrible job,

00:20:38.560 --> 00:20:40.500
but why couldn't you play along?

00:20:40.500 --> 00:20:41.840
That's mean!

00:20:42.600 --> 00:20:43.940
I'm back.

00:20:43.940 --> 00:20:46.130
You can go home, Koyuki-kun.

00:20:46.130 --> 00:20:47.580
And here's a little gift.

00:20:47.580 --> 00:20:49.100
Thank you.

00:20:49.260 --> 00:20:52.340
From our perspective,
it may be a little embarrassing

00:20:52.340 --> 00:20:54.340
for him to think that would actually work.

00:20:54.340 --> 00:20:55.640
But for Gestöber,

00:20:55.640 --> 00:20:57.950
it was the best decision he 
could make in light of his job.

00:20:58.070 --> 00:21:00.150
Who do you think you are?!

00:21:00.150 --> 00:21:02.840
Never come back again, jerk!

00:21:02.840 --> 00:21:06.630
Oh, this is my favorite brand of coffee beans!

00:21:06.630 --> 00:21:08.160
Gestöber!

00:21:08.160 --> 00:21:10.300
Aww, Seri-kun's such a tsundere!

00:21:10.300 --> 00:21:12.200
Best friends forever!

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:13.930
RIP
Koyuki

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:14.840
<i>I yelled at Hanadori-kun again...</i>

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:16.440
RIP
Koyuki

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:16.520
RIP
Koyuki

00:21:12.200 --> 00:21:18.920
RIP
Koyuki

00:21:14.500 --> 00:21:18.920
<b><i>Resignation</i></b>

00:21:15.280 --> 00:21:18.930
<i>And I quit my new job that same day.</i>

00:22:49.440 --> 00:22:52.400
<i>After quitting my job in 
a fit of youthful rashness,</i>

00:22:52.400 --> 00:22:55.200
<i>I don't have the funds to 
buy Sumiso-san a present.</i>

00:22:55.900 --> 00:22:58.200
<i>My beloved Nyanteko...</i>

00:23:05.610 --> 00:23:07.190
<b>Squeeze</b>

00:23:07.290 --> 00:23:09.120
Oh, Seri-kun.

00:23:09.120 --> 00:23:12.220
You're not going to give her
 a drooly, dirty, stinky

00:23:09.530 --> 00:23:15.580
<b>Drooly</b>

00:23:10.130 --> 00:23:15.580
<b>Dirty</b>

00:23:10.760 --> 00:23:15.580
<b>Stinky</b>

00:23:12.220 --> 00:23:15.590
present like <i>that</i>, are you?
Are you trying to put her off?

00:23:16.390 --> 00:23:17.300
Stop it!

00:23:17.300 --> 00:23:20.420
Don't ruin anything else that's precious to me!

00:23:20.420 --> 00:23:22.350
I'm not giving it to her, okay?!

00:23:22.820 --> 00:23:24.450
Also, when did you get in my house?

00:23:24.920 --> 00:23:39.930
<b>Don't look for me</b>

00:23:25.790 --> 00:23:28.460
This is no good. I haven't slept in a week.

00:23:28.460 --> 00:23:30.440
I'm quitting the anime industry.

00:23:30.440 --> 00:23:31.600
I'm out of options!

00:23:31.600 --> 00:23:32.990
What's wrong, Gestöber?

00:23:32.990 --> 00:23:34.580
Your enemy is my enemy!

00:23:34.580 --> 00:23:37.280
I, Sturmhut, will chase away 
all disasters that befall you!

00:23:37.280 --> 00:23:39.260
This was <i>your</i> idea!
